works: In the spring the letter comes, and by the autumn {N} has a new study, a great congregation and a diary with no empty evenings in it.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the decision still feels right a year later, and the people {N} serves say so.
fails: The panel thanks {N} warmly and chooses {rival}, and {N} goes home the long way, rehearsing what might have been said.
fails: The year does not go as planned, and {N} is left with less time, less certainty and the same cold building.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6. the order chooses its head (pairs D1b)
# The summit, a step at real odds: every colour's way of being chosen is a try for [head of a faith order] at 6, for a
# [senior cleric] or a [member of a monastic community] of six years or more (the summit refines both, so the title
# fits everyone who meets the moment). Not a long shot, so no perk on failure. The pairs, all at 85, are the honest
# other ways through an election: a season at the order's poorest house, the strongest candidate backed early, an open
# letter to the order, a term asked for the head, and a turn given to an older colleague. Every colour's mean is 45.5.

== the order chooses its head
tier: life event
