likelier: a flock that follows, a name known across the country, a degree in theology, long years in the order, the old head's death or retirement
rarer: a junior post, a faith that chooses its heads from elsewhere, a council already split
gap: 8-20
domain: faith.5
tone: mixed
life: faith, publiclife
horizon: months
roles: boss, rival, mentor, colleague
earth: the head of the faith order has died after thirty years, and the council meets to choose who comes next
tribal: the great shaman whom every band heeds has died, full of years, and the keepers of the rites gather to choose who comes next
magic: the high priest of the god's order has died, and the order's council gathers in the great temple to choose the next
scene: The old head of the order died in the spring, full of years, after thirty years in office, and the council will meet at midsummer to choose who comes next. Three names are spoken of in the corridors, and {Ns} is one of them. {rival} has been travelling to every house of the order since the funeral; {mentor}, who has seen two of these elections, says the council always surprises itself.
scene W: The order chooses its head by a rule nearly a thousand years old: a vigil, a vote, and a second vote if the first is split. {N} has always kept the rule and will keep this one.
scene U: {N} has been thinking for years about where the order must go: the empty houses, the young who come and do not stay, the money. Nobody else seems to have a plan at all.
scene B: Fourteen votes on the council, and eight make a head. {N} can count six already.
scene R: {N} is tired of the careful talk in the corridors. The order is shrinking, and somebody should say so out loud.
scene G: {N} goes on with the day: prayer at dawn, the garden, the sick at the house in the town. If the order wants {N}, it knows where to look.
scene tribal: The great shaman whom every band heeded has died, full of years, and at midsummer the keepers of the rites will gather at the sacred place to choose who comes next. {Ns} name is spoken at the fires; {rival} has walked to every band since the burial.
scene magic: The high priest of the god's order has died, and at midsummer the order's council will gather in the great temple to choose the next. Three names are whispered in the cloisters, and {Ns} is one; {rival} has visited every house of the order since the funeral rites.
