# ================================================================ long shot

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 8. a sermon that goes round the country (triads D3b)
# Someone records a sermon and it spreads, for a minister, a lay teacher of the faith or a street preacher with three
# years or more behind them (`tenure: 3-99`; LIFE_CALLINGS_LONGSHOTS gate: not a senior cleric yet). Luck opens the
# next rung, at 3 in every colour, each single with `grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed` (core/longshot.py):
# [senior cleric] for the minister (U the sermon made a series, B the fortnight of fame used, G the city brought to
# the flooded town; `requires: ordained religious minister | without: impossible`), and ordination, the faith's leaders
# asking them to train, for the lay teacher (W, the full training; `requires: lay religious teacher`) and the street
# preacher (R, yes to the call and the street kept; `requires: street preacher`), each `without: impossible`, as
# art-longshots.lib does, so that nobody is offered a try at a title already held. A requires: names one rung, so each
# of the two non-ministers sees one single, and the minister three; the five triads, all at 84, are what everyone
# meets: the sermon written out for the congregation, the faith's own office to put it out properly, talks only
# nearby, the gifts it brings given to the flooded families, a week of answers and then back to the work. Every
# colour's mean is 43.5.

== a sermon that goes round the country
tier: life event
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-95
holds: ordained religious minister | lay religious teacher | street preacher
tenure: 3-99
per_year: 0 0 0 .01 .01 .005
drivers: era+.2 fortune+.3
times: per minister, lay teacher or street preacher with three years or more behind them, a year: about 1 in 100 has a sermon or a talk recorded and shared far beyond their own congregation (estimate); sermons and talks are shared online by the thousand every week, and only a handful a year lead to a great congregation's call or to ordination (estimate); about 4 lives in 1,000 are ministers, 3 in 100 lay teachers of the faith and 5 in 1,000 street preachers (catalogue shares)
likelier: a sermon on something everyone is feeling that week, someone in the seats who films it well, years of preaching behind it, a time when people are looking for words
rarer: a quiet week, a sermon only the congregation would understand, a preacher nobody records
gap: 6-15
domain: faith.5
tone: joy
life: faith, publiclife
horizon: week
roles: friend, boss, mentor, colleague, rival
earth: someone films a sermon on a phone, by the end of the week it has gone round the whole country, and the faith's leaders are writing
tribal: a telling at the fire is carried by traders from band to band down the whole river, and the keepers of far bands send for the one who spoke it
magic: a sermon preached in a small chapel is copied by the printers and read aloud in every city of the realm, and letters come from the great temples
scene: On an ordinary rest day {N} spoke about the flood that had taken half the town's houses that month: twelve minutes, no notes, on what people owe each other when the water comes. {friend} filmed it on a phone and posted it that night. By Friday it has been watched two million times, a newspaper has rung, and two letters lie on the table: one from a great congregation in the city, one from the faith's leaders, who would like to talk about {Ns} future.
scene W: {N} reads the faith's letter twice. It asks for a meeting, properly, and talks about training and a future in the faith. {N} would like to answer it properly too.
scene U: {N} watches the sermon for the first time and tries to see what two million people heard in it: the plainness, perhaps, or the timing. It is worth understanding before saying anything else.
scene B: Attention like this lasts a fortnight, and letters like these do not come twice. {N} knows which one leads further.
scene R: {N} still means every word of it, and the hundreds of messages from strangers make {N} want to preach it again tomorrow, louder.
scene G: The people in the sermon are the town's own: the baker who opened her shop to the flooded, the farmer with the tractor. {N} thinks the sermon belongs to them more than to anyone.
scene tribal: {N} spoke at the fire of the flood that took the low camp, and of what each hearth owes the others when the water comes. Traders carried the telling down the river, and now runners come from far bands: their keepers of the rites want to hear the one who spoke it.
scene magic: {N} preached in a small chapel on the flood that took the lower town, and a clerk copied it down. The printers have sold it in every city of the realm, and two letters lie on the table: one from a great temple of the capital, one from the order's council.
