- UBR | answer the messages for one week, then switch the phone off and go back to work | v: self-direction, security | tribal: sit with the runners for one moon, then send them home and go back to the band's rites | magic: answer the letters for one week, then shut the door and go back to the chapel | foot: lesson attention passes, the work stays | chance: 84
works: Within a month the letter that matters has a date in it, and {N} stands in a much larger room, with the same twelve minutes still going round.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the sermon goes on doing good where it landed, and {N} is glad to have preached it.
fails: The talk dies down after ten days, something else takes everyone's attention, and the meeting with the faith's leaders is warm and comes to nothing.
fails: The panel listens politely and says {N} is a wonderful preacher, which is not the same as a yes.

# ================================================================ world-only (magic)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9. the god speaks in the temple (only: magic; pairs D6a)
# The magic crossing to the summit: the temple's oracle says the god has chosen a new high priest. For a priest of a
# great temple ([senior cleric]), each one-colour way is a try for [head of a faith order] (high priest of a god's
# order) at its real chance, 6 (`requires: senior cleric | without: impossible`, so a priest without a great temple
# meets the five pairs alone, as art-worlds.lib does). Black's way pays the oracle to speak the name (someone else's
# power, never the priest's own gift), at 15, with the price on a closed: approval: line and its backfire: the god's
# favour is a debt. The pairs are the honest ways: the council asked to keep the law of choosing, the oracle's past
# buyers named in open council, an older and better priest put forward, an open refusal of a choice bought from an
# oracle, a month of prayer in the temple garden. They form a ring (each colour in two), so their chances are solved
# around the singles (66 and 84) until every colour's mean is 40.5. per_year is the brief's; LIFE_CALLINGS gates it
# (three years a priest of a great temple, or ten a priest).

== the god speaks in the temple
tier: life event
only: magic
stages: adult mature elder
age: 45-100
holds: senior cleric | ordained religious minister
tenure: 3-99
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .02 .01
drivers: fortune+.2 community+.1
times: per priest of a great temple, or priest of ten years, in the magic world a year: about 1 in 60 is at the temple when the oracle says the god has chosen a new high priest (estimate); in many old faiths an oracle or a sign was asked before a high priest was chosen, and the council did not always follow it (estimate); about 5 lives in 10,000 are priests of a great temple (catalogue share)
likelier: an old high priest failing, a priest known for devotion, a feast year, a council already divided
rarer: a young high priest in good health, a temple far from the god's seat, a priest the oracle has spoken against
gap: 8-20
domain: faith.5
tone: mixed
life: faith, publiclife
horizon: months
roles: boss, rival, mentor, colleague
magic: the temple's oracle says the god has chosen a new high priest, and will speak the chosen name to the council for a price
scene magic: On the feast of the god the oracle in the inner court goes into her trance before the whole temple and speaks: the god has chosen a new high priest from among those present, and will make the choice known. That night a temple servant brings {N} word that the oracle will speak {Ns} name to the council, for a price she will name herself. {rival}, it is whispered, has already been to her. The order's council meets at the new moon.
scene magic W: The order chooses its high priest by its council and its law, and the god has always spoken through that law. {N} is uneasy at any word that comes round the side of it.
scene magic U: Oracles have spoken before, and the council's archive records how often their words came true. {N} goes down to the archive that night to read them.
scene magic B: The price will be high, and so is the seat. {N} weighs what the oracle could ask, and what a high priest could pay back.
scene magic R: {N} felt something in the court when the oracle spoke, a stillness like the moment before a storm. Whatever it was, {N} wants to meet it head on.
scene magic G: The god chose the grandmother of {Ns} grandmother to serve, the family says, and the god chooses in its own seasons. {N} would rather wait for the god than buy its word.
- W | wait for the council's vote, and stand by the order's law of choosing | identity | title: head of a faith order | requires: senior cleric | without: impossible | v: conformity, tradition | chance: 6
- U | read the archive's record of every oracle, and lay the truth of it before the council | self_control: + | title: head of a faith order | requires: senior cleric | without: impossible | mark: learned a skill | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 6
- B | pay the oracle's price, and let her speak your name to the council | title: head of a faith order | requires: senior cleric | without: impossible | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: the oracle's price, paid behind the council's back; backfire: the god's favour is a debt, and in the first year the oracle comes to collect it | self_control: - | v: power, achievement | chance: 15
- R | stand before the oracle in the inner court, and ask the god to its face | title: head of a faith order | requires: senior cleric | without: impossible | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 6
- G | go on with the daily offices, and leave the choice to the god's own season | title: head of a faith order | requires: senior cleric | without: impossible | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 6
- BG | put forward an older and better priest, and stand at their right hand | door | grants: friend in power | v: benevolence, security | chance: 66
- UG | spend the month before the council praying and listening in the temple garden | habit | v: tradition, self-direction | foot: place faith.seeking | chance: 84
- UR | find out who has paid the oracle before, and say so in open council | mark: made an enemy | v: universalism, stimulation | chance: 66
- WB | ask the council to rule that no oracle's word may decide the choosing | v: conformity, power | foot: lesson the law outlasts any oracle | chance: 66
- WR | refuse openly to serve any high priest whose seat was bought from an oracle | mark: defied an authority | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 84
works: At the new moon the council chooses, the bells ring across the city, and the temple settles into the new high priest's years.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the season of the oracle passes, and the order's council does its work in peace.
fails: The council chooses {rival}, and nobody speaks of the oracle's word again.
fails: The oracle's season splits the council, the choosing drags on for a year, and {N} is left out of the end of it.
